   $q$The narrator calls the quiet in the cafeteria a "deafening silence." What does this oxymoron suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The quiet was so intense that it felt almost as powerful as a loud noise.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The players could not hear anything because their ears were covered.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The cafeteria was actually very noisy during the tournament games.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The silence lasted only a moment before the players began talking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The quiet was so intense that it felt almost as powerful as a loud noise.$q$, $q$Joining "deafening" and "silence" shows how strongly Tobias feels the quiet; he becomes "aware of every breath he took." The passage says the only sounds were clicks and taps, so the room was not actually noisy.$q$, 'draft', '248dda41-945b-504d-807d-6115bfb9063e')
