   $q$The coach says Tobias "found a creative way to give away a bishop." What is the role of this euphemism?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It points out a clear mistake gently, with humor that Tobias can laugh at.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It harshly scolds Tobias so that he will quit the chess team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It explains that the bishop was taken because Priya broke a rule.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It sincerely praises Tobias for inventing a brilliant new chess strategy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It points out a clear mistake gently, with humor that Tobias can laugh at.$q$, $q$"Creative" softens the fact that Tobias simply lost a piece, and his laughter shows he "knew exactly what the coach meant." Reading it as sincere praise misses the gentle joke; he lost the game, so the move was not brilliant.$q$, 'draft', '248dda41-945b-504d-807d-6115bfb9063e')
