  ('3c66edfd-0354-50a2-89a0-44ef5295bd55', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author writes that the plant "hides from the sun's heat while still collecting its energy." How does this sentence connect to the idea of the name "living stones"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that the plant needs no sunlight because it is like a stone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows another paired opposite: the plant both hides like a stone and gathers light like a living thing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests the plant prefers shade and is usually found in forests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that the plant is mostly dead and survives only by luck.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows another paired opposite: the plant both hides like a stone and gathers light like a living thing.$q$, $q$The sentence balances hiding with collecting, echoing how the plant is both stone-like and alive. The window exists precisely so sunlight can reach the plant, so claiming it needs no sunlight contradicts the paragraph.$q$, 'draft', 'e7e59545-576f-5455-8b37-f3bcf51196e8')
