  ('f6ca7673-503e-57ef-bc59-c0b6b3826e0d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The final paragraph calls the plant "the quiet stone" and says it returns to its "patient disguise." What effect do these words have?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They suggest the plant is lazy and will not bloom unless someone waters it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"They explain that the plant makes noise only while it is flowering.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They give the plant humanlike qualities, presenting its survival as calm, steady waiting.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They show the plant becomes a real stone after its flower fades away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They give the plant humanlike qualities, presenting its survival as calm, steady waiting.$q$, $q$"Patient" and "quiet" personify the plant, matching its long wait "for the next rain." "Patient" has a positive connotation, unlike "lazy," and the passage gives no sign that it needs a person to water it.$q$, 'draft', 'e7e59545-576f-5455-8b37-f3bcf51196e8')
