  ('237a3724-a407-509e-a622-b1a138e50419', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author praises the merchant's "stubborn imagination." What is the effect of pairing these two words?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the merchant was creative only when he was working alone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It criticizes the merchant for refusing to listen to good advice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It combines persistence with creativity, turning a usually negative word into praise.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests that the merchant had many ideas but never acted on them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It combines persistence with creativity, turning a usually negative word into praise.$q$, $q$"Stubborn" often sounds negative, but beside "imagination" it praises his refusal to quit after "disappointing" first voyages. He clearly acted on his ideas, solving melting with sawdust and building demand.$q$, 'draft', 'a64d80fc-e58f-572f-aac4-f572782d3a6c')
